{{Quote|The Noghri are said to be fearsome warriors. With those sharp teeth and claws I don't doubt it!|An artist, in [[Unidentified artist's journal|his journal]]|<ref name="Alien Archive" />}}
The '''Noghri''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Honoghr]]. They had [[Color|gray]] skin, a row of horns on their head and ran on all fours. Noghri were known for their combat skills and keen sense of smell.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|It's a lot like a Sinrich optical dephaser, but it's got a totally different design. Looks like it's limited to three minutes on a charge, doesn't work on humans— needs a Noghri's double-layer skin conductivity or something— and doesn't cover any added stuff one it's been activated.|Sergeant Drav notes Noghri double-layer skin conductivity|<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances" />}}
[[File:Noghri_SWR.png|thumb|left|180px|Rukh, Grand Admiral Thrawn's assassin]]
The Noghri were [[humanoid]] in shape, with a torso, a single head, two [[Limb|arms]] and two legs. Entirely [[hair]]less and wiry, they had [[Color|gray]] skin and a row of short horns atop their heads. Their hands and feet each possessed four long digits.<ref name="Kindred" /> Although they stood upright, walking with a [[Primate|simian]] gait, the Noghri ran on all fours and were capable of leaping great heights and jumping long distances. They were also gifted with a keen sense of smell.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|noghri|Noghri}}</ref>

==Noghri in the galaxy==
Because of their strong sense of smell and advanced combat skills, Noghri were often employed as trackers and assassins.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> [[Rukh]] was a [[Gender|male]] Noghri [[assassin]] who often worked for Imperial [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]].<ref name="Rukh">{{Databank|rukh|Rukh}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Noghri made their first [[canon]] appearance in the comic [[Rogue One - Cassian & K-2SO Special 1|''Rogue One - Cassian & K-2SO Special'' 1]], wherein one Noghri was present on [[Wecacoe]] when [[Captain]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] [[Mission to Wecacoe|traveled there]] to extract [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] security protocols.<ref name="Cassian & K-2SO">[[Rogue One - Cassian & K-2SO Special 1|''Rogue One - Cassian & K-2SO Special'' 1]]</ref> However, these events would later be contradicted by [[Andor Season 2|''Andor'' Season 2]], which detailed an alternate story for how Andor met the droid [[K-2SO]].<ref name="Who Are You?">{{Andor|Who Are You?}}</ref>

